## 5. ROOT / OPERATOR STEPS NOT PERFORMED

No sudo was invoked at any point in this run, and nothing below was attempted.
Listed in dependency order so a later sitting can resume from step 0.

  0. ON THE LAPTOP, by hand at the machine (not scriptable from here):
       System Settings > General > Sharing > Remote Login = ON
     Verify from the rig:  ssh -o BatchMode=yes MikoBook.local 'uname -m'

  1. ON THE RIG (control plane) — the running server has NO --mesh-ip, so it must
     be reinstalled onto a mesh IP before any worker can join. This TEARS DOWN the
     live single-node cluster currently serving the M11 vm-path work; coordinate
     before running it.
       sudo /Library/k3sm/k3sm install server --mesh-ip <cp-mesh-ip>
       sudo launchctl kickstart -k system/io.k3sm.server      # if already installed
       /Library/k3sm/k3sm token create                        # mint the join token

  2. ON THE LAPTOP (worker):
       # stage the binary and the conformance helpers first — native pods exec a
       # HOST binary path and there is no image distribution (hack/lab/m3.sh:93-96)
       scp /Library/k3sm/k3sm MikoBook.local:/tmp/k3sm
       ssh MikoBook.local 'sudo install -m 0755 /tmp/k3sm /Library/k3sm/k3sm'
       ssh MikoBook.local 'sudo /Library/k3sm/k3sm install agent \
             --server <cp-mesh-ip> --token <join-token> --node-ip <worker-mesh-ip>'
       # then mirror $K3SM_CONFORMANCE_BIN (default /tmp/k3sm-conformance-bin)
       # from the rig to the SAME path on the worker

  3. BACK ON THE RIG, re-run this gate:
       KUBECONFIG=$HOME/.kube/config K3SM_LAB=1 hack/lab/m3.sh \
         | tee hack/lab/runs/m3-lab-local-<UTCdate>.log

  RESUME-AFTER-ROOT: hack/lab/m3.sh itself needs NO root — it is pure kubectl plus
  the e2e suite against $KUBECONFIG. Every root step above is CLUSTER BRING-UP,
  which the gate's header (lines 26-30) explicitly declares out of scope
  ("Prerequisites (manual two-Mac setup, NOT done here)"). So the resume flow is
  simply step 3: once the two nodes are up, the gate is re-runnable unprivileged
  by an agent. There is no partial-progress state to carry across the root steps.

  EXPECTED RESULT OF STEP 3 TODAY: m3.0 goes GREEN (two Ready nodes) and m3.A goes
  RED, for the two named causes in section 4 (B213 unlanded => the apiserver
  rejects :10250, so in-pod kubectl fails; M14.2 unlanded => the server has no
  mesh device, so the cross-node path carries no traffic). Performing the root
  steps does not by itself turn this gate green.

